cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this as an AI-assisted structural research note, not as a solution of Erdős Problem #64."
title: "Excess-Sensitive Degree-Three Bounds for Minimal Erdős–Gyárfás Counterexamples"
type: dataset
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-06
authors:
  - family-names: "Loevseth"
    given-names: "Zackary"
    alias: "ZackaryLoevseth"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZackaryLoevseth/Erd-s-Problem-64"
url: "https://github.com/ZackaryLoevseth/Erd-s-Problem-64"
abstract: >-
  AI-assisted structural research on hypothetical lexicographically minimal
  counterexamples to the Erdős–Gyárfás power-of-two cycle conjecture. With
  A=V_3(G), B=V_{>=4}(G), b=|B|, and s=sum_{v in B}(d(v)-4), the public note
  proves |A| >= 2b+s+4 and derives 3|A| >= 2|V(G)|+s+4 and
  |E(G)| <= 2|V(G)|-b-2. Erdős Problem #64 remains open. The proof has
  internal AI-assisted reconstructions but no external specialist review;
  novelty and priority are not claimed.
keywords:
  - graph theory
  - Erdős–Gyárfás conjecture
  - power-of-two cycles
  - minimal counterexample
  - degree sequence
  - degeneracy
  - AI-assisted mathematics
